<article class="env-lemma" id="2FEF7F">
  <p><a class="environment-identifier" href="/tag/2FEF7F">Lemma <span data-tag="2FEF7F">2.4.4.8</span>.</a> Suppose given a diagram of simplicial sets </p>
  <div class="equation">
  \[  \xymatrix { \bd \Delta ^ n \ar [r]^{f_0} \ar @{^{(}->}[d] &amp;  X \ar [d]^{p} \\ \Delta ^ n \ar @{-->}[ur]^{f} \ar [r]^{g} &amp;  S } \]
</div>
  <p> where $p$ is a Cartesian fibration and $n > 0$. Suppose that $f_0(0)$ is an initial object of the $\infty $-category $X_{g(0)} = X \times _{S} \{  g(0) \} $. Then there exists a map $f: \Delta ^ n \rightarrow S$ as indicated by the dotted arrow in the diagram, which renders the diagram commutative. </p>
</article>
<article class="env-proof">
    <p>
      <strong>Proof.</strong>
      Pulling back via $g$, we may replace $S$ by $\Delta ^ n$ and thereby reduce to the case where $S$ is an $\infty $-category and $g(0)$ is an initial object of $S$. It follows from Lemma <a href="/tag/70D9EC" data-tag="70D9EC">2.4.4.7</a> that $f_0(v)$ is an initial object of $S$, which implies the existence of the desired extension $f$. 
      <span class="qed">$\square$</span>
    </p>
</article>